# Citation File Format 1.2.0 — https://citation-file-format.github.io/
# GitHub reads this file and exposes a "Cite this repository" button on the
# repo homepage, which produces APA / BibTeX citations in one click. Zotero,
# Mendeley, and other reference managers also pick this up automatically.
#
# Bump `version` and `date-released` on each release; keep them in sync with
# package.json and src/lib/citations.ts (WORKBENCH_VERSION).

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software in academic or published work, please cite it
  using the metadata below. Primary citations should still go to the
  underlying corpus sources (GORILA, mwenge/lineara.xyz, John Younger's
  scholarly material) — see the in-app Research Report's Citation block
  for one-click pre-formatted entries covering all of them.
type: software
title: Linear A Research Workbench
abstract: >-
  A browser-based computational research environment for the Linear A
  corpus — the undeciphered Bronze Age Minoan script (ca. 1800–1450 BCE).
  Includes 50 interactive modules covering cross-linguistic phonetic
  alignment, sign concordances, scribal paleography links, accounting
  verification, lexical and graphotactic statistics, hypothesis testing,
  and publication-ready report export.
authors:
  - family-names: Pavlicek
    given-names: Ryan
version: 1.5.1
date-released: "2026-06-14"
url: "https://github.com/ryanpavlicek/linearaworkbench"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ryanpavlicek/linearaworkbench"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - Linear A
  - Minoan
  - undeciphered scripts
  - Bronze Age Aegean
  - corpus linguistics
  - computational philology
  - digital humanities
  - epigraphy
